  "body": "## What changed\n\n`reenter` in `crates/motion/src/machining3d/reentry.rs` handles a pass restart in a 3D Pocket level. This PR changes its branch for a tool that is not centre-cutting:\n\n- If the full disc is proved clear, the restart plunges. This is unchanged.\n- If the core is not cleared (M11.3 core law, `plunge_law::into_solid`), the M11.3 fallback runs: helix, then the ramp along the pass, else the named refusal. This is unchanged.\n- If the core is cleared but the outer disc is not proved clear, the fallback now runs on a copy of the path. The copy is kept if it has no refusal and is clean (no plunge into uncut stock, no crossing of a posted move). Otherwise the restart plunges, and a note names the plunge.\n\nThe centre-cutting branch is unchanged. The decision is in `docs/decisions/3885-non-cc-reentry.md`.\n\n## Cause\n\n#3857 applied the full-disc test to all tools. For a tool that is not centre-cutting, a restart over a cleared core then went to the M11.3 fallback. Where no helix or ramp fits, that fallback refuses the operation. Before #3857, the same restart was a legal plunge by the core law. So the change refused a legal program.\n\n## Tests\n\nThe new pins are in `crates/motion/src/machining3d/reentry.rs` (`camcraft-motion` lib). Each test calls `reenter` with a hand-built level. The tool has a radius of 3 mm and is not centre-cutting.\n\n- `machining3d::reentry::tests::a_non_centre_cutting_restart_over_a_cleared_core_plunges_without_room`: an earlier cut 1 mm from the axis clears the core. No helix or ramp fits. The test asserts no refusal, a plunge, and the note. It is red on unchanged upstream/main with this text: `entry refused: the tool is not centre-cutting - a pass start inside the level, and no helix or ramp fits onto Z -1.000`.\n- `machining3d::reentry::tests::a_non_centre_cutting_restart_over_a_cleared_core_prefers_an_entry`: the same restart with room takes a helix or ramp, with no plunge into the material.\n- `machining3d::reentry::tests::a_non_centre_cutting_restart_over_solid_core_is_refused_without_room`: the earlier cut is 2 mm from the axis, outside the 1.5 mm core reach. The refusal stays, with its name.\n\nMutation results:\n\n- Upstream code: `..._plunges_without_room` fails. The fix makes it pass.\n- Remove the `refused` guard: `..._plunges_without_room` fails.\n- Skip the core-law check (`if false`): `..._over_solid_core_is_refused_without_room` fails.\n- Always plunge over a cleared core (the old core-only law): `..._prefers_an_entry` fails.\n- The fix is restored after each mutation, and all 5 `reentry` tests pass.\n\nCommands on the final head `9ba125988`, against upstream/main `b13f790ec`:\n\n- `cargo xtask gate quick --base upstream/main`: GREEN. 51 steps, 0 failed, 0 stalled. This includes `app suites: example_catalog`, `example_catalog_adaptive`, `example_catalog_edge_work`, and `pocket3d_pass_start` (motion and app).\n- `cargo xtask gate light --base upstream/main`: GREEN. 6 steps, 0 failed.\n- `cargo clippy -p camcraft-motion --all-targets -- -D warnings`: GREEN.\n\nThe heavy lanes did not run. AGENTS.md \"Heavy lanes at review\" gives a `P3` PR no heavy step.\n\n## Goldens moved\n\nNone. The catalog suites ran in the quick gate and passed. After the gate, `git status` showed no changed `*.nc`, `*.cl` or `examples/catalog/**` file. No catalog case uses a non-centre-cutting tool at a restart over a cleared core.\n\n## Not exercised\n\n- No end-to-end fixture through `pocket3d` reaches the \"cleared core, no room\" case. The pins call `reenter` directly. This is the pattern of `crossing_hop_tests.rs`.\n- No machine run. No screenshots, because the change has no UI effect.\n\n## Overlaps\n\nNone on `reentry.rs`. Open PR #3880 changes `crates/motion/src/machining3d/descent.rs`, and #3869 changes `ladder.rs`. This PR changes neither file.\n\nChangelog: 3D Pocket: a pass restart with a tool that is not centre-cutting no longer refuses the operation when the earlier cuts cleared the tool's core; it takes a helix or ramp where one fits, else the named plunge.\n\nEffort: high\n\nFixes #3885\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n",
